      "id": 2,
      "claim": "The observed frequency equals the emitted frequency (no Doppler shift) exactly when v_o = v_s (both have the same speed component along the line of sight and in the same direction).",
      "evidence": "Setting f' = f in the formula gives (v + v_o) = (v - v_s) → v_o = v_s.",
      "weight": 0.30,
      "depends_on": [1]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "claim": "Option (C) – both source and detector travel in the same direction – can satisfy v_o = v_s if they move with equal speeds.",
      "evidence": "Choosing equal speeds makes the velocity components along the line of sight identical, fulfilling the condition from step 2.",
      "weight": 0.20,
      "depends_on": [2]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "claim": "Options (A), (B), and (D) cannot satisfy v_o = v_s while respecting the described motions, so a Doppler shift must occur in those cases.",
      "evidence": "In (A) the observer is stationary (v_o = 0) while the source moves (v_s ≠ 0); in (B) the source is stationary (v_s = 0) while the observer moves (v_o ≠ 0); in (D) the source and observer move in opposite directions, giving v_o = –v_s, not equality.",
      "weight": 0.15,
